== The rule that makes tables feel like a real editor (doc 18) ==
A Shift-selection is a TEXT selection while the moving end stays in ONE cell, and
PROMOTES to a CELL-BLOCK selection the instant it crosses into another cell -- driving
exactly one of the two INDEPENDENT a11y mechanisms (ITextRangeProvider text range vs
per-cell kSelected / ISelectionProvider2) and firing the matching event.

